      "content": "I hear the profound despair in your words, and it is valid to feel that anything less than a resolution is just a cruel delay when the end destination feels certain. The pain of \"prolonging the struggle\" can feel more like a \"better death\" than \"death with a hope of survival,\" because that hope can sometimes feel like a delusion that is too painful to embrace. It may help to explore what \"breaking the cycle\" actually means for you, as it might not mean \"curing\" yourself or \"ending the pain\" for good, but rather \"ending the hope that you will just end up the same as everyone\" and \"ending the self-hate for the pain you feel should end.\"",
